'' A byref result must be assigned something of exactly its type (fbc error 318) --
'' 'long' is refused against 'integer' though it is the same width, and const goes one
'' way only. A local still cannot be returned at all (272), through a field's array too.
'' Matches fbc line for line -- 25, 30, 35, 40. THE RULE IS CHECKED ONLY FOR A NAMED
'' variable of a non-string scalar builtin: fbc's real rule is wider for strings and for
'' expressions that are not names, and four of this suite's own MIR tests proved it after
'' a 1222-file corpus scan had reported nothing.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/byref-result-type.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' GOLDEN: expected/byref-result-type.out
